NYC Payroll Data Integration Pipeline
Project Report

Author: Alankriti Mehra
Project Category: Data Engineering
Technologies: Azure Data Factory, Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2, Azure SQL Database

1. Introduction

The NYC Payroll Data Integration Pipeline is a cloud-based data engineering project developed using Microsoft Azure.

The purpose of this project is to demonstrate how payroll data can be ingested, organized, transformed, and stored using Azure cloud services.

The project uses Azure Data Factory to orchestrate data integration workflows, Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 for data storage, and Azure SQL Database for structured data storage and verification.

2. Project Objectives

The main objectives of this project are:

Build an automated data integration pipeline using Azure Data Factory.
Load agency, employee, and title master datasets.
Ingest NYC Payroll datasets for 2020 and 2021.
Create a payroll summary dataset.
Store processed data in Azure SQL Database and Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2.
Verify successful pipeline execution and data availability.
3. Technologies Used

Azure Data Factory

Used to create and orchestrate data integration pipelines, configure linked services, manage datasets, and execute data workflows.

Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2

Used as a cloud storage service for storing project data.

Azure SQL Database

Used for structured data storage and SQL-based data verification.

SQL

Used to create database tables and support the project's data storage and verification requirements.

4. Project Architecture

The project follows a cloud-based data integration architecture.

The workflow involves:

Preparing the NYC Payroll datasets.
Configuring connections through Azure Data Factory linked services.
Defining datasets for the required data sources and destinations.
Creating pipeline activities and data flows.
Loading agency, employee, and title master data.
Loading Payroll 2020 and Payroll 2021 data.
Creating the payroll summary dataset.
Storing processed data in Azure SQL Database and Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2.
Verifying data availability and pipeline execution.
5. Implementation
5.1 Linked Services

Configured linked services in Azure Data Factory to establish connections with the required Azure data services.

5.2 Datasets

Created datasets to represent the data used throughout the integration workflow.

5.3 Data Flows

Configured data flow components to support the project's data processing and transformation workflow.

5.4 Pipeline Development

Developed an Azure Data Factory pipeline to coordinate the ingestion and processing of the NYC Payroll datasets.

The pipeline handles master data, payroll datasets for 2020 and 2021, and payroll summary generation.

5.5 SQL Database Setup

Created SQL scripts to prepare the required database tables, including agency, employee, payroll, and summary-related tables.

6. Data Verification

The project includes verification activities to check the availability of processed data.

The following verification evidence is included:

Azure Data Factory pipeline execution screenshots.
Activity execution screenshots.
Azure Data Lake Storage verification screenshots.
SQL database verification screenshots.
Dataset and linked service configuration screenshots.
7. Project Outcomes

Through this project, I developed practical experience in:

Designing cloud-based data integration workflows.
Working with Azure Data Factory.
Configuring Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2.
Using Azure SQL Database.
Creating SQL database tables.
Understanding data ingestion and transformation workflows.
Monitoring pipeline execution and verifying stored data.
8. Challenges and Learning

This project provided practical exposure to integrating multiple Azure services into a data engineering workflow.

It helped strengthen my understanding of cloud data storage, pipeline orchestration, dataset configuration, SQL database management, and data verification.

9. Conclusion

The NYC Payroll Data Integration Pipeline demonstrates the use of Microsoft Azure services to build a cloud-based data integration workflow.

By combining Azure Data Factory, Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2, and Azure SQL Database, this project provides practical experience in data ingestion, processing, storage, and verification.

It represents an important step in developing my cloud data engineering skills.

